mpanies that really align with your  values as opposed to like i'm just going  to get the first job that i can do  employees have the upper hand these days  do you think i do think so and i think  what you're also seeing is that the  employers companies are really taking a  look at not only do i how do i get  people to come join the company because  we have all these job openings how do i  get them to stay  so it's become a culture of more  human-centric and if you see like we  just released our jobs on the rise and a  lot of the jobs that are you know rising  to the top are ones that are really  indicate that companies are looking for  this so diversity inclusion managers  chief  hr officers and the talent acquisition  specialist so they're starting to really  invest in those these are jobs with  college degrees involved  yes generally speaking but there are  also like in logistics which is we see  is an industry that is hiring a lot and  what's great about that  is that they offer training and they pay  well so this is an area where people who  are shifting industries maybe they don't  want to be burned by the hospitality  industry i do want to deliver on the  promise of that jerry maguire clip how  should one  gracefully exit a job they no longer  want to be in yes you have to keep in  mind that the relationships that you've  built during your career and at that job  are going to carry you through your job  so that is walk out singing take this  job and shove it is that good i would  not do that that is not good advice and  so you really want to you know leave a  job just as you joined it gracefully and  with the intention to build and maintain  those relationships and let make sure  your boss is the first to know give  adequate you know notice with the demand  for um  jobs that require you to work from home  or allow you to work from home which  states are hiring well we're seeing a  lot of interest in denver and cleveland  and austin and some of this could be  